    "Costs are estimates (recorded tokens x list prices), not invoices.",
    "Old IMR dropped: structured fields only, near chance, superseded by Persius. Recorded IMR rows are retained for audit.",
    "Latency is observed client wall time including router pacing and retries; speed ratios are deployment-specific.",
    "Native calibration and the automation cutoff use the selected-class probability; live routing uses the API confidence scalar, which can differ.",
    "Frontier confidence is self-reported by the model; Drex confidence is a native probability. ECE, Brier and reliability bins are never pooled across the two.",
    "Human/hard-cap routed questions are not model answers: they are excluded from model accuracy and counted as not correct in the all-scored view, never as human success.",
    "The 1% automation threshold is selected on the dev split only; test rows are used only to evaluate the fixed cutoff.",
    "Synthetic upper bound: the same team wrote the documents and the labels."
